# Side nav ↔ operative console (invariant)

In `loot&lasers/Scenes/Main/game_shell.gd`, the **operative console** and **side nav** are permanently coupled.

## Contract

1. **Operative console** (portrait, name, currencies, XP) is fixed-height chrome at the top of the rail (`SIZE_SHRINK_BEGIN`). It must **not** expand into nav space.
2. **All page buttons** (currently 15) live in the leftover height **under** the console and must stay **fully visible at every window height** — **never** put the page list in a `ScrollContainer`.
3. **Equal buttons**: every page button shares the same height and the same in-group spacing. Keep **group headings** (Explore / Social / Battle / Trade) and **slightly larger gaps between groups** than between buttons inside a group.
4. Stretch groups by **item count** so 3-button groups (Battle) still yield the same per-button height as 4-button groups.
5. **No minimum** button height or font floor — if the console grows or the window shrinks, buttons rescale to fit.
6. Changing the console must only change leftover nav height (buttons rescale). Changing nav must not force the console to grow, scroll, or reflow.

## Do not

- Reintroduce scroll for page nav
- Give page buttons a non-zero `custom_minimum_size.y` that causes clipping/cutoff
- Give the operative panel `SIZE_EXPAND_FILL`
- Remove group headings or flatten all gaps to one uniform value unless the user asks

## Baseline look

Preserve today’s console + nav visual scale (fonts, icons, portrait, rail width) unless the user explicitly changes the console; then only the nav button heights may change as a consequence.
